 "id": "H-0073",
 "title": "Deferred checkpoint restart: JOB RESTART=(stepname,checkid) with a SYSCHK DD before the first EXEC, RD=R and SYSCKEOV on the checkpointed step",
 "category": "jcl",
 "issue": 4891,
 "shapes": [
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDCHK.jcl: JOB statement carries RESTART=(CHK020,C0000012); //SYSCHK DD DSN=PROD.BDLD.CHKPT,DISP=(OLD,KEEP) sits between the JOB statement and the first EXEC",
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDCHK.jcl CHK020: EXEC PGM=SORT,RD=R with a //SYSCKEOV DD (end-of-volume checkpoint data set)"
 ],
 "asserts": "RESTART=(step,checkid) on the JOB statement is the restart of every jcl_steps fact in that job (the step name) and restart_checkid names the checkpoint inside that step. SYSCHK is a job-level DD: a jcl_dds fact with step null, dd SYSCHK, dsn PROD.BDLD.CHKPT, disp OLD, disp_normal KEEP. RD=R is the rd of the jcl_steps fact of the EXEC that codes it. SYSCKEOV is an ordinary DD of CHK020. The steps before the restart step are not run.",
 "citations": [
